          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ساحل (sāḥil) is built on the native Arabic root s-ḥ-l, \"to scrape, to pare\" (Lane). Lane gives sāḥil as the shore; Swahili comes from its plural sawāḥil, \"coasts\"."
            }
          ]
        },
